hibtrace - diagnostic kernel module used 2026-11-14 to find why hibernate froze
at power-off on this ROG Zephyrus G16 (GU605MI). Not loaded normally.

While loaded it logs entry/return of the core hibernate path and the NVIDIA
PM/shutdown functions, and arms a watchdog when hibernation starts. If
hibernation is still running after watchdog_secs, it prints every blocked
task's stack and every CPU's backtrace, then panics, so the log lands in
firmware storage (EFI pstore) and the laptop restarts by itself.
Needs: sysctl kernel.panic=10 and efi_pstore enabled (GRUB:
efi_pstore.pstore_disable=0).

Build:  make -C /lib/modules/$(uname -r)/build M=$PWD LLVM=1 modules
Use:    sudo insmod hibtrace.ko watchdog_secs=120 ; (hibernate) ; sudo rmmod hibtrace

After a panic, systemd-pstore archives the records at the next real boot
(/var/lib/systemd/pstore). After a hibernate *restore* the pstore filesystem
does not list them; read them straight from
/sys/firmware/efi/efivars/dump-type0-*-cfc8fc79-be2e-4ddc-97f0-9f98bfe298a0
(skip the 4-byte attribute header, then raw deflate: zlib.decompress(d, -15)).

Finding: cs35l56_hda_system_suspend -> __flush_work waits for
cs35l56_hda_dsp_work -> request_firmware -> btrfs read that never completes
during hibernation (btrfs read completion runs on freezable workqueues).
It is memory-dependent because hibernation evicts the page cache to make room.
Fix: /usr/lib/systemd/system-sleep/30-cs35l56-hibernate detaches the amps for
the hibernate step only. the health check (configs/usr/local/bin/g16-doctor) verifies the fix is still in place.

Lessons:
- Never write the RTC from here. A CMOS-year step marker made the clock jump
  to 2115 on resume, because the kernel adds 100 years to two-digit years under
  70 on top of the firmware century byte.
- Calling non-exported kernel functions by a kprobe-looked-up address oopses
  under CET IBT ("Missing ENDBR").
- Runtime tracepoint_printk does nothing unless tp_printk was on the cmdline.

Evidence: docs/findings/01-hibernate-hang-cs35l56.md
